    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῑκᾰνία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <u>Sicania</u>, old name of Sicily
		as inhabited by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σικανοί</span> (afterwards of
		the part they inhabited, <i><span class="en">
			St.Byz.
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			24.307
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σ. ἡ νῦν Σικελίη καλευμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.170
				</span></i>
			:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῐκᾰνός</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐκᾰ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				57
			</span></i>], ὁ, <i>a Sicanian</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philist.
				3
			</span></i>, etc.: Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῐκᾰνικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.62
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῇ Σ. τῆς Σικελίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					359b15
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σικάνῃ</span>
			).</div>
